{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774738,"nonce":"J0rR/A9hVEj5m16E5+yvxo2uEa8=","title":"fix(observability): count forge set_status failures; bound the quiet PodInitializing loop (ba921db, c653742)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #80 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/dogfood-silent-forge-status-and-tail-spam` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-25T18:05:19Z · Merged: 2026-07-25T18:14:43Z\n\nCloses git-bug `ba921db` and `c653742`. Two commits, one per ticket.\n\n**Both tickets were already half-fixed on `main` on 2026-07-18** and never closed. Rather than redo them, this closes the second-order gap each earlier fix left behind.\n\n---\n\n**Already there** (`32f42a0`): the structured `warn!` with repo/run/sha/forge-error, `record_outbox_failure`, `dead_letter_outbox` at `MAX_DELIVERY_ATTEMPTS = 10`, and a `checks.rs` test using `FakeForge::failing_status()`. The poison bound is genuinely covered — there is no hot-loop left, and a PG contract test already asserts it.\n\n**Still missing: a metric.** The store cannot recover this after the fact — a rejected status row looks identical to an untried one, so `scarab_outbox_depth` can't separate \"busy\" from \"permanently broken\". A GitHub App missing `statuses:write` was invisible on a dashboard.\n\nAdds `crates/scarab-server/src/metrics.rs` — process-lifetime counters rendered alongside the existing pull-model gauges on `GET /metrics`:\n- `scarab_forge_status_failures_total`\n- `scarab_forge_status_dead_lettered_total`\n\nCounters rather than gauges because these are events that leave no distinguishing state behind; process-global because the increments happen in the converged driver's outbox drain, which has no `AppState`.\n\nThe existing test now asserts the counter **delta** across the drain loop (2 messages × 10 rejections, then 2 dead-letters), so a rejection can no longer vanish uncounted. `observability.rs` asserts the series is exposed at 0 in a fresh process, so an alert can be written before the first failure.\n\n---\n\n**Already there** (`e1b67d3`): `is_pod_not_ready()` matching the specific benign reasons `PodInitializing` / `ContainerCreating` — deliberately *not* the generic \"is waiting to start:\" prefix — dropped to `debug!`.\n\n**Still missing: a bound.** A Pod that never starts its container (wedged init container, volume that never mounts) now retries **silently forever**, so \"this step has no logs\" has no explanation anywhere. Quiet-forever is the mirror image of the reported bug.\n\nAdds a pure policy function:\n\n```rust\nclassify_tail_error(err, not_ready_for, since_last_warn) -\u003e Quiet | StuckNotReady | Failed\n```\n\n- inside `NOT_READY_GRACE` (180s) → quiet (debug)\n- past it → WARN naming `not_ready_for_s` and what to check, rate-limited to one line per 60s\n- a genuine error → WARN immediately, regardless of elapsed time\n\n`LogTailer` gained a per-fence `not_ready` map, cleared when the tail drains cleanly or hits a different failure. Four unit tests assert the policy directly rather than scraping log output.\n\n---\n\n`cargo check -p scarab-server --all-targets` clean · `-p scarab-server --lib --test log_tail --test tail_lease --test checks --test observability` = 49 passed · `rustfmt --check` clean on every touched file, no repo-wide `cargo fmt`.\n\nIntegrated with the other three dogfood branches: **597 passed, 21 ignored** with `SCARAB_TEST_REQUIRE_PG=1`.\n\nScope is `crates/scarab-server` only — no `ForgePort` or `Db` signature change, and the log pipeline itself (`pump_log_stream` / `LogService`) is untouched; only the error-reporting policy around the drain moved.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}